    intel_pstate_update_max_freq(all_cpu_data[cpu]);

Reason: The loop iterates over all possible CPUs, but offline CPUs have `all_cpu_data[cpu]` set to NULL. Passing this NULL pointer to `intel_pstate_update_max_freq` (which takes a `struct cpudata*` and immediately dereferences `cpudata->cpu`) causes a NULL pointer dereference.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
static bool intel_pstate_update_max_freq(int cpu) {
    struct cpufreq_policy *policy __free(put_cpufreq_policy) = cpufreq_cpu_get(cpu);
